Z||000005||TheFiero64||02-25-2001||03:18 PM||||I am shocked that the piston didn't shoot out of the caliper and stop all the brakes from working way before it got that bad. Some people never cease to amaze me. I thought I've seen it all.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>88 Coupe V6<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/TheFiero64_signature1.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Wolfhound||02-25-2001||03:38 PM||||The brakes on this car work now! I drove it around the yard and my long dirt drive way to check out the transmission. <BR> I know the person who wrecked the car and it went of the road to the right in a left hand curve. I,m pretty sure the brake contributed to the wreck.||||reg||1
Z||000007||My7Fieros||02-25-2001||08:12 PM||||My Formula was like that when I bought it. NO rear rotors! They had not only seperated from the "drum" part, but had split in two!<BR>New rotors from the Fiero Store and a rear caliper rebuild kit from Autozone quickly remedied that problem though. <BR>Wow, I thought I was the only one who had ever encountered that problem!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://tgowens.com/My7Fieros_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
